[40.134559, "o", "    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  qwen3.6-35b — 10 tool call(s) so far\r\n  │ `ensurepip` is available. Let me use it to restore pip.\r\n[approval] bash: python3 -m ensurepip --upgrade 2>&1 — approved\r\n  ⚙ bash python3 -m ensurepip --upgrade 2>&1\r\n    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  qwen3.6-35b — 11 tool call(s) so far\r\n[approval] bash: pip3 --version 2>&1 — approved\r\n  ⚙ bash pip3 --version 2>&1\r\n    ✗ bash — exit 1\r\n  qwen3.6-35b — 12 tool call(s) so far\r\n  │ Hmm, `ensurepip` says it's already satisfied but the module still isn't i…\r\n[approval] bash: python3 -m ensurepip -v --upgrade 2>&1 — approved\r\n  ⚙ bash python3 -m ensurepip -v --upgrade 2>&1\r\n    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  qwen3.6-35b — 13 tool call(s) so far\r\n[approval] bash: ls /usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pip/ 2>&1 | head -10 — approved\r\n  ⚙ bash ls /usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pip/ 2>&1 | head -10\r\n    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  qwen3.6-35b — 14 tool call(s) so far\r\n  │ The wheel exists in a temp dir but `ensurepip`"]
[40.13467, "o", " thinks pip is already inst…\r\n[approval] bash: rm -rf /usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pip-24.3.1.dist-info && python3 -m ensurepip --upgrade 2>&1 — approved\r\n  ⚙ bash rm -rf /usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pip-24.3.1.dist-info &&…\r\n    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  qwen3.6-35b — 15 tool call(s) so far\r\n[approval] bash: pip3 --version 2>&1 — approved\r\n  ⚙ bash pip3 --version 2>&1\r\n    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  qwen3.6-35b — 16 tool call(s) so far\r\n[approval] bash: pip3 install --dry-run requests 2>&1 — approved\r\n  ⚙ bash pip3 install --dry-run requests 2>&1\r\n    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  qwen3.6-35b — 17 tool call(s) so far\r\npip is fully working again. Here's what was wrong and what I did:\r\n\r\n**Problem:** The `pip` package's actual source code (`/usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pip/`) was missing from your system, but the stale metadata directory (`pip-24.3.1.dist-info/`) remained. This made `ensurepip` think pip was already installed and skip re-extracting it, so `pip3` would a"]
[40.134698, "o", "lways fail with `ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'pip'`.\r\n\r\n**Fix:** I removed the orphaned `.dist-info` directory and re-ran `python3 -m ensurepip --upgrade`, which extracted the bundled pip wheel back into place. pip 24.3.1 is now functional and can install packages.\r\n\r\n[refusal] role=implementor model=qwen3.6-35b tools=17 surface=d1e34a72922b\r\n"]
